  "description": "The latest Juice 29er hardtail frame features practical updates to its feature set and geometry without wading too deep into progressive geometry. Seat tube angle is slightly steeper for easier climbing, but it isn't super slack and low. It is a bike you can still ride with \"old-school\" techniques, but also can be ridden with a modern technique if you pick the right size and parts. We wanted the Juice to excel at rolling terrain and long days in the saddle bike packing. Not everybody wants or needs a bike optimized mainly for descending black diamond trails.\n\nOn this smooth-riding steel frame, you'll find lots of braze-ons and bosses for utiliity, industry standards like 148mm Boost hub spacing and English threaded bottom bracket shell. IRD Broski sliding dropouts not only give you the option to run your bike as a single speed, with a geared hub, or derailleurs, but allows you to select a shorter or longer rear center – longer for more stability while loaded, shorter for more natural handling on singletrack.\n\nGeometry is optimized for 100mm travel 29″ forks and will handle 120mm forks great, too\n\nLatest update adopts Boost 12 x 148 thru-axle hub standard\n\nED coating under paint and inside tubes to resist rust\n\nS-bend seatstays and chainstays\n\nRear rack and fender eyelets\n\n31.6mm post size/34.9mm frt. der. size/34.9mm seat collar/73mm bottom bracket (English threads); 400mm+ post(rigid) recommended\n\nSizes: SM(39cm), MD(42cm), LG(46cm), XL(51cm)\n\nStart with the customer – find out what they want and give it to them.",
